## Scope

Author requests a Zotero patch, not a Zoteus workaround. Target the
document-worker reference index and `isReferenceBlock`, as shipped in Zotero
10.0.1. This is a local implementation ticket; no upstream issue or PR has
been sent.

For B eligible blocks and R bibliography runs, the current membership query
scans the runs before consulting a Set: worst-case O(B × R). Build a Set of
run root references once with the reference index, then test membership with
the same equality semantics. Preserve the existing nested reference-block Set
fallback. Expected work becomes O(R + B), with O(R) additional index space.
Do not silently replace citation selection or change extraction semantics.

## Evidence and acceptance

- Source audit: `verification/SDT-PALGRAVE-AUDIT.md`.
- Exact-function counter probe:
  `verification/probes/sdt_reference_membership.mjs` and
  `bench/results/sdt-diagnostic-2026-09-05/reference-membership.json`.
- Phase measurements: `verification/SDT-PALGRAVE-PHASES.md`. The scan is
  demonstrated, but its share of total citation time is not isolated.
- Re-read current document-worker source and open changes before patching.
- Differential tests cover matching/nonmatching roots, nested references,
  malformed references, empty indexes and index construction/mutation.
- Count operations while independently scaling blocks and bibliography runs.
- Compare native decoded packs on identical fixtures, excluding creation date.
- Measure citation-stage time without promising a whole-pipeline linear bound.
- Any upstream filing follows `GOVERNANCE.md` and explicit authorization.
